My notes:

It looks like there is an issue with the movement at the end of melee combat. In round 2 Unit A moves from position -5 to -4 when it should have moved from -5 to -6. In round three Unit A consolidates from position -5 to -2
which is correct. The issue seems to be that the movement doesn't take into account that backwards for units that start in the negative should be to make their ending position more negative than their starting position.
The round 2 example for Unit A it should have moved from -5 to -6. 



